### Buzzer scoring and answer opportunity

The administrator must be able to configure:

- Marks for the first correct answer.
- Negative marks for an incorrect answer.
- Marks for an unanswered question.
- Whether the next participant in the queue gets an opportunity after an incorrect answer.
- Maximum number of answer attempts per question.
- Time allowed to answer after buzzing.
- Whether the buzzer can be activated again after all participants in the queue have answered.

Suggested default scoring:

- Correct answer: +10 marks.
- Incorrect answer: -5 marks.
- No answer within the permitted time: configurable, default 0.

The queue must preserve the original order in which participants pressed the button.

### Technical requirements for buzzer functionality

- Use real-time server synchronization rather than relying on mobile-device clocks.
- Use an atomic server-side transaction or equivalent mechanism to establish the order of buzzer presses.
- Prevent duplicate buzzer registration from the same participant for the same question.
- Provide immediate visual and vibration feedback on the participant's phone wherever supported.
- Disable the buzzer immediately when the quizmaster deactivates it.
- If a participant presses the buzzer after it has been deactivated, do not register the press.
- Lock the buzzer automatically when the configured response window closes.
- Record the exact order of accepted presses for transparency.
- Display connection status for every participant.
- Handle network delays and disconnections without silently changing an already registered queue.

The platform must be tested on multiple actual mobile devices simultaneously. It must not determine the winner simply by using the local device's timestamp.

## 2. IDENTIFY THE SOUND ROUND

- Play an audio clip on the main display.
- Participants must identify the sound, drug, instrument, song or phenomenon.
- Allow the quizmaster to configure the number of audio attempts.
- Provide a sound playback and replay control.
- Allow the answer to be given verbally or through the buzzer.
- Scoring must be configurable.

## 3. IDENTIFY THE VIDEO ROUND

- Display a short video clip.
- Participants must identify the subject or answer a question based on the video.
- Support common video formats.
- Allow the quizmaster to pause, play and replay the clip.
- Provide configurable answering time and marks.

## 4. CONNECT THE CLUES ROUND

- Display two or more clues sequentially.
- Participants must identify the common connection.
- Allow the quizmaster to reveal clues one at a time.
- Configure marks according to the number of clues required.
- Allow negative marking.

## 5. JUMBLED WORD ROUND

- Display jumbled letters representing a scientific term, drug name, scientist, disease or pharmaceutical concept.
- Participants must identify the correct word.
- Support a timer and configurable scoring.
- Allow the quizmaster to reveal the answer.

## 6. TRUE OR FALSE ROUND

- Present statements on the main screen.
- Participants can answer using their mobile interface or verbally, as configured.
- Award marks for correct responses.
- Configure negative marking if required.

## 7. MULTIPLE-CHOICE ROUND

- Display four options on the main screen.
- Allow participants to answer through their mobile phones or provide verbal responses.
- Configure individual or simultaneous response modes.
- Automatically evaluate answers when mobile response mode is selected.

## 8. PASS-ON ROUND

- One participant receives a question.
- If unable to answer, the participant can pass the question.
- The next eligible participant gets an opportunity.
- Configure the marks awarded to the first participant and subsequent participants.
- Allow the quizmaster to control the passing sequence.

## 9. BONUS / DOUBLE-POINTS ROUND

- Provide questions carrying special marks.
- Allow the administrator to define bonus points or double-point multipliers.
- Display the special scoring rule prominently.
- Apply the configured scoring automatically.

## 10. WAGER ROUND

- Allow participants or teams to wager a selected number of marks before the question is revealed or answered, according to the selected rules.
- Set minimum and maximum wager limits.
- Configure winnings and losses.
- Display the final score adjustment transparently.

All optional rounds must be independently configurable and must not interfere with other rounds.

# PART 5: PARTICIPANT REGISTRATION AND MOBILE INTERFACE

## 1. Participant registration

The administrator must be able to add:

- Participant name.
- Team name.
- Roll number or participant ID, if applicable.
- Institution or department.
- Mobile number, if required.

Provide a QR code and unique joining code for each quiz.

Participants should be able to join through their mobile phone browser without installing a separate application.

Once registered, each participant should see only their own mobile quiz interface.

## 2. Mobile participant interface

Design a clean, minimal interface.

During regular rounds, the participant can simply observe the main screen and await their turn.

During buzzer rounds, display a large, easily accessible button:

**BUZZ IN!**

When the buzzer is inactive, the button must remain disabled.

When the quizmaster activates the buzzer, it becomes active automatically.

After the participant presses it:

- Immediately show a confirmation message.
- Display their registered position in the buzzer queue, if available.
- Prevent repeated presses for the same question.
- Show the result of their response when the quizmaster concludes the buzzer sequence.

Do not reveal the correct answer to participants before the quizmaster announces it.

# PART 6: LIVE LEADERBOARD AND SCORING SYSTEM

Create an automatic scoring engine.

The system must calculate scores independently for every participant or team.

For example:

| Team | Round I | Round II | Round III | Round IV | Round V | Total |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Team Alpha | 40 | 40 | 50 | 30 | 35 | 195 |
| Team Beta | 50 | 30 | 40 | 40 | 30 | 190 |
| Team Gamma | 30 | 50 | 40 | 25 | 40 | 185 |

These figures are illustrative.

Requirements:

- Update scores immediately after the quizmaster evaluates an answer.
- Maintain separate scores for every round.
- Automatically calculate the cumulative score.
- Reflect positive and negative marks correctly.
- Display the current leaderboard.
- Allow the quizmaster to show or hide the leaderboard after each round.
- Provide a final leaderboard showing all participants or teams in descending order of marks.
- Support tied scores.
- Provide a configurable tie-breaker round.
- Maintain a complete score-change history.
- Record manual corrections with the date, time and reason.

The scoring engine must use the settings configured for the active quiz and round. It must not apply fixed scoring rules from another quiz.

# PART 7: QUESTION BANK AND QUESTION MANAGEMENT

Create a dedicated question bank for every quiz.

Allow the administrator to:

- Add questions manually.
- Import questions from Excel or CSV.
- Add multiple-choice questions.
- Add descriptive or verbal-answer questions.
- Upload images.
- Upload audio clips.
